{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PCDc9TPupYMAyhbdjDATV2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives formal specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity against GNU reference binaries through differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility Go binaries), `pkg/sys/` (platform syscall wrappers), `pkg/format/` (shared output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential test harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists on the working branch for `pkg/format/` (color.go, column.go, size.go), `pkg/sys/` (fileinfo.go, fileinfo_darwin.go, fileinfo_linux.go, terminal.go), and `pkg/testutils/` (difftest.go, difftest_test.go). No `cmd/` code is on the working branch. Tests exist for `pkg/testutils/` but not for `pkg/format/` or `pkg/sys/`.\n\n**Current release (00.0)**: Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure. Four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles: magefiles/ excluded by DD7; only cmd/version/ is a generation target (no code yet)\n- uc002-format: implementation exists, **tests missing**\n- uc003-sys: implementation exists, **tests missing**\n- uc004-testutils: implementation and tests both exist\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest incomplete release. Of its four use cases, testutils is complete (code + tests), format and sys have implementations but no tests, and magefiles has cmd/version pending. Per P8 ordering (libraries before consumers, alphabetical tiebreak), `pkg/format/` tests come before `pkg/sys/` tests, and both come before `cmd/version/`. Proposing format tests first.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd003-format R1, R2, R3 -- unit tests for pkg/format\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (full requirement set for format package)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test cases for release 00.0 including format)\n      - pkg/format/color.go (ANSI color output implementation to test)\n      - pkg/format/column.go (column alignment implementation to test)\n      - pkg/format/size.go (human-readable size formatting implementation to test)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go (reference for project test conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n      - path: pkg/format/column_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for Columns, PadRight, PadLeft\n      - path: pkg/format/size_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for HumanSize with binary and SI unit systems\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test column alignment functions per prd003-format R1: Columns distributes entries into the maximum number of columns fitting within termWidth with per-column widths and 2-space gap (R1.1, R1.4); PadRight and PadLeft pad strings to specified display widths and return unchanged when already wider (R1.2); display width uses rune count (R1.3)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test ANSI color output per prd003-format R2: FileTypeColor returns correct escape sequences for each file type -- directory (blue), symlink (cyan), executable (green), block device (yellow bold), char device (yellow bold), socket (magenta), pipe (yellow) -- and empty string for regular files (R2.1, R2.4); Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color enabled and empty string when disabled (R2.2); ColorEnabled returns true only for TTY-backed writers (R2.3); SetColorEnabled forces color on or off regardless of TTY (R2.6); ResetColorEnabled reverts to auto-detection (R2.7)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test human-readable size formatting per prd003-format R3: HumanSize converts byte counts to human-readable strings matching GNU coreutils human_readable() behavior (R3.1); binary mode uses 1024-based units with K/M/G/T/P/E suffixes (R3.2); SI mode uses 1000-based units with kB/MB/GB/TB suffixes (R3.3); values under 10 at a scaled unit show one decimal place, values at or above 10 show integer format, zero returns \\\"0\\\" (R3.4)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Test files mirror source files per project convention established in pkg/testutils/: color.go -> color_test.go, column.go -> column_test.go, size.go -> size_test.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Color tests call SetColorEnabled(true) to force color on without requiring a real TTY, then call ResetColorEnabled() in test cleanup to restore auto-detection, per prd003-format R2.6 and R2.7\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"All tests use table-driven subtests with t.Run, following the pattern established in pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/format/... passes with all tests green\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"color_test.go covers FileTypeColor for all 7 file types (directory, symlink, char device, block device, socket, pipe, executable) plus regular file returning empty string, and covers SetColorEnabled/ResetColorEnabled override behavior\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"column_test.go covers Columns with empty input returning nil, single entry, entries fitting multiple columns, and entries requiring single-column fallback; covers PadRight and PadLeft for strings shorter than, equal to, and wider than the target width\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"size_test.go covers HumanSize for zero bytes, byte-range values below 1024/1000, values crossing at least two unit thresholds, and values under and over 10 at scaled units, in both Binary and SI modes\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33843,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33843},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c39c4ba-692f-438b-adc9-77c158d6c6d2","uuid":"8ab67bc2-6dad-48c1-8e51-f74b39ecbea9"}
